// Analyzed file list for nvdla_rubik_merge_transpose. Paths are relative to the
// PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as cwd
// and `slang` is run from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd. Do not add a trailing `-y`/library directive after the file list --
// an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// One `analyze -sv12` covers the whole list, which is what the upstream task
// did too: the generated RUBIK RTL is Verilog-2001 but declares no identifier
// that SystemVerilog-2012 reserves.
//
// No `+incdir+`: unlike the other four nvdla packages this one ships no
// `include/` directory. `simulate_x_tick.vh` is not reached from the RUBIK
// core, and the upstream task's analyze line carries no include path either.

// `SYNTHESIS` selects the synthesizable branch of the generated RTL. The
// upstream task passes no `VLIB_BYPASS_POWER_CG` here because this package
// ships no clock gate: the RUBIK core's only instantiated cell is the RAM.
+define+SYNTHESIS

// --- the RAM model ----------------------------------------------------------
// nv_ram_rws_32x16_functional.sv is the task's functional replacement for the
// nv_ram_rws_32x16 foundry/DFT wrapper. The module it declares is
// `nv_ram_rws_32x16`, which is the name the RUBIK core instantiates 32 times.
rtl/nv_ram_rws_32x16_functional.sv

// --- the RUBIK register-file core, byte-identical upstream RTL --------------
rtl/NV_NVDLA_RUBIK_rf_core.v

// --- the oracle and the formal top ------------------------------------------
sva/nvdla_rubik_merge_transpose_checker.sv
ft/nvdla_rubik_merge_transpose_ft.sv

// ---- phase-1 candidate targets ----------------------------------------
// LAST, because it is a `bind` into nvdla_rubik_merge_transpose_ft and a bind
// must be analyzed after the module it binds into.
sva/targets_nvdla_rubik_merge_transpose.sv
